## Const generics (ADR 0954, gen.const.1 to gen.const.3): a const argument `4` is the type
## `Struct("4")` (no source can declare a struct of that name), bound to its
## parameter in `gen.tsubst` like a type, and an instance is named with it
## (`Vec[float, 4]`). The parameter `N` read as a value is the constant.

## Whether `name` is a written const argument: digits.
fn is_const_arg(name str) bool
    name.len() > 0 and "0123456789".contains(name.slice(0, 1))

## The value of const parameter `name` in the instance being lowered.
fn Lower.const_param_value(mut self, name str) Val?
    t := gen.tsubst.get(name)?
    n := match t
        Struct(s) => if is_const_arg(s) then s.to_int() else none
        _ => none
    k := n?
    Val(id: konst(k, Ty.Int), ty: Ty.Int)
